  "details": "VRChat version : Build 1134\nEdit : I noticed that in my world this bug is related to Unity, not VRChat, the parent GameObject had a scale bigger than one, by setting it to one the issue dissapeared.\n\nThis is something I started noticing two days ago in many world, including mine.\nPickable objects tend to move on the z-axis without external force, see this short video showing two examples : https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GZnbgpx9Jjg (first clip was taken in MERoom)\nThat bug is actually very hard to reproduce, sometimes it happens, sometimes it doesn't, but basically I just took the pickable object and dropped it, then it started moving from alone, but it doesn't always happen.\nIn my world (second example in the video above) I have a similar issue, the door tends to slide on the z-axis.",
